# Reuse Before Create

**Before writing a new component, utility, or UI pattern**, you MUST:

1. **Search the codebase** for existing implementations that do the same or similar thing (e.g. pagination, modals, tables, search inputs, row actions, form patterns).
2. **Reuse the existing one** if it fits (same app or shared package). Pass props or adapt the call site; do not copy-paste and rename.
3. **If the same pattern exists in multiple places** (e.g. several `*-pagination.tsx` or `*-modal.tsx` files with nearly identical logic), **extract or use a single generic component** and migrate all callers to it. Do not add another one-off copy.

## Shared pieces in the Hermes dashboard

Paths are under `apps/hermes/dashboard/`. Primitives (Button, Card, Table, Sheet, Dialog, Sidebar and so on) live in `@workspace/ui` (`packages/shared/ui`); add missing ones with `npx shadcn@latest add <name>` from `apps/hermes/dashboard`, never by hand.

| Need | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Page title, description and actions | `components/page-header.tsx` (`PageHeader`) |
| Key facts on a detail page | `components/summary-grid.tsx` (`SummaryGrid`, `SummaryItem`) |
| Any date or time | `components/date-time/date-time.tsx` (`DateTime`), formatted in the viewer's zone |
| List table frame and sortable headers | `components/data-table/data-table-card.tsx`, `components/data-table/sortable-header.tsx` |
| Pagination | `components/list-pagination.tsx` (`ListPagination`) |
| Status pills | `components/status-badge.tsx` (`StatusBadge`) |
| Confirm before a destructive action | `components/confirm-action-dialog.tsx` (`ConfirmActionDialog`) with `hooks/use-confirm-action-dialog.ts` |
| Create/edit modal state | `components/entity-form-modal-provider.tsx` |
| Modal form layout | `components/form-dialog.tsx`, `components/submit-button.tsx`, `components/form-error-alert.tsx` |
| One-time secret display | `components/one-time-secret-reveal.tsx` |
| Copyable id | `components/copyable-id.tsx` |
| Execution detail pages | `components/execution-detail/` (`ExecutionDetailView`) |
| Execution list cells | `components/execution-history-cells.tsx` |
| Manifest-driven domain detail | `components/detail-blocks/` |

- **Modals / forms:** if create and edit are almost the same, use one component with a mode or discriminated props (for example `variable={null}` for create and `variable={row}` for edit). Do not add separate `AddXModal` and `EditXModal` that duplicate the form and submit logic.
- **Tables, search, row actions:** search for the existing pattern under `app/dashboard/` and reuse or generalize it before writing a new variant.

```
❌ BAD — duplicate pattern
- User asks for pagination on a new list page.
- You create NewFeaturePagination.tsx that again implements prev/next, query string, aria-label.

✅ GOOD — reuse first
- Search for "pagination" / "Pagination" in the app.
- Use the existing ListPagination (or equivalent) with the right basePath and ariaLabel.
- If none exists but the same pattern appears in 2+ files, extract one shared component and switch callers to it.
```
